A||N||4||kornholio||Audio experts: bass tube subwoofer recommendations||||5
Z||000000||kornholio||10-26-1999||06:05 PM||||How does a bass tube subwoofer sound in a Fiero?  88 Fiero, you mentioned that you had 2 Bazookas behind the seats.  What model number is it?  Is anyone else using a tube sub?  I would like to get a Bazooka or some similar all-in-one unit rather than a factory sub or a custom setup because of the price.  And building one is out of the question, as I would have no idea what I'm doing (that's another reason I would like an all-in-one unit).  What other companies make subs like the Bazookas?  What's the cheapest one I can find?  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88 Fiero||10-26-1999||06:22 PM||||kornholio...my Bazookas size are 5 1/4 and fits perfectly nice behind the seats both driver and passenger...I am 6'2 and I still seat comfortably in the car.. You can feel the base and it sounds good. You probably want to give the Bazooka Company a call.. I know that you can't buy these tube sizes anymore but then they might make an exeptions...good luck!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||88 Fiero||10-26-1999||06:22 PM||||kornholio...my Bazookas size are 5 1/4 and fits perfectly nice behind the seats both driver and passenger...I am 6'2 and I still seat comfortably in the car.. You can feel the base and it sounds good. You probably want to give the Bazooka Company a call.. I know that you can't buy these tube sizes anymore but then they might make an exeptions...good luck!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||10-26-1999||07:13 PM||||I have 1 sony Xplode 10" sub in a hatch box where your spare tire is. The spare is in the trunk. It is powered by a jensen 300x1 amp bridged to 400 watts. It bumps fairly well because of the sealed off space. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||10-26-1999||09:24 PM||||kornholio, my buddy has 2 6.5" Hollywood Sound Labs tubes in his car (velcroed in front of each seat).  these offer a wonderfull amount of base (i have felt my insides pulse), i cannot remember what size amp he has pushing them with, i believe it was a 30 or 50 watt rms US Amp.  very clean crisp sound!||||reg||1
